<!DOCTYPE html>
<!--
  The template of /app/licenses/crates.html (ADR 0042). cargo-about renders it
  with about.toml; scripts/crate-notices.sh runs it in the Containerfile's rust
  stage and in the PR check. Handlebars escapes every {{value}} for HTML, so a
  licence text can never inject markup; no value here uses the unescaped
  triple-brace form.
-->
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Licence notices of the crates in backend3-cli</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: sans-serif; line-height: 1.4; max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; }
  th, td { border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f6f6f6; padding: 0.75rem; overflow-x: auto; }
  .note { font-style: italic; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Licence notices of the crates in backend3-cli</h1>

<p>
  <code>/app/backend3-cli</code>, the program of this image, is website_backend3
  (<a href="https://github.com/Verseghy/website_backend3">source</a>), licensed
  AGPL-3.0-only. It is built with Rust and links the third-party crates below.
  This file lists every third-party crate in the binary's dependency graph for
  <code>x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu</code>, without build scripts' and tests'
  dependencies, with its version, its licence and the licence text. The
  procedural macros that run while the binary compiles are listed too.
  cargo-about wrote this file from <code>Cargo.lock</code> when the image was
  built. The source of each crate is published on crates.io at the version
  listed, which the links below open.
</p>
<p>
  Beside this file, in <code>/app/licenses/</code>: <code>README.txt</code>,
  which lists every file of the directory; <code>notices/</code>, the
  <code>NOTICE</code> files that crates under the Apache License 2.0 ship, which
  <code>README.txt</code> lists;
  and <code>COPYRIGHT-library.html</code>, the notices of the Rust standard
  library from the toolchain that built the binary. The notices of the npm
  packages bundled into the admin UI are in
  <code>/app/admin/dist/licenses.txt</code>.
</p>

<h2 id="ijg-statement">The Independent JPEG Group</h2>
<p>This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.</p>

<h2 id="overview">Licences</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{id}}): {{count}}</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

<h2 id="crates">Crates</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Crate</th><th>Version</th><th>Licence</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{#each crates}}
<tr><td>{{package.name}}</td><td><a href="https://crates.io/crates/{{package.name}}/{{package.version}}">{{package.version}}</a></td><td>{{license}}</td></tr>
{{/each}}
</tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="texts">Licence texts</h2>
{{#each licenses}}
{{#if first_of_kind}}
<h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}} ({{id}})</h3>
{{/if}}
<section id="{{id}}-{{@index}}">
<p>Used by:
{{#each used_by}}
  <a href="https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a>{{#unless @last}},{{/unless}}
{{/each}}
</p>
{{#if source_path}}
<p class="note">The text of the crate's own licence file.</p>
{{else}}
<p class="note">The standard text of the licence: these crates ship no text of it of their own, so it names no copyright holder.</p>
{{/if}}
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
</section>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
